From: local build patch <zjgunks@gmail.com>
Subject: sing-box: make naive (cronet) outbound configurable

SING_BOX_BUILD_NAIVE_OUTBOUND is a def_bool y, i.e. hard-wired on for
every architecture outside the mips list. It force-selects libcronet,
whose build downloads a Chromium x86_64-only clang toolchain, so any
build on a non-x86_64 host (e.g. arm64) fails unconditionally.

Turn the switch into a user-visible bool with default y so existing
(x86_64) builds keep naive/cronet enabled unchanged, while hosts that
cannot run the Chromium toolchain can opt out explicitly.

--- a/net/sing-box/Makefile
+++ b/net/sing-box/Makefile
@@ -80,7 +80,8 @@
   depends on $(subst @,,$(GO_ARCH_DEPENDS))
 
   config SING_BOX_BUILD_NAIVE_OUTBOUND
-  def_bool y
+  bool "build naive (cronet) outbound"
+  default y
   depends on !(arc||armeb||loongarch64||mips||mips64||powerpc||TARGET_gemini)
 endef
 
